{
  "_about": [
    "Cross-language parity fixture for the targeting-rule bucketing algorithm.",
    "The same JSON is loaded by:",
    "  - backend/framework/experimentation/src/test/kotlin/.../TargetingBucketingFixtureTest.kt",
    "  - web/analytics/src/feature_flags_bucketing.spec.ts",
    "Each side computes its own bucketing using its own implementation of the",
    "FNV-1a 64-bit hash + sorted-weight bucket walk and asserts that the",
    "result equals `expectedVariation` for every row. Any drift between the",
    "Kotlin and TS implementations therefore fails CI on whichever side did",
    "not change in lockstep with the other.",
    "",
    "Algorithm:",
    "  1. seed = `${flagKey}:${salt}:${ruleId}:${identifier}` (UTF-8 bytes)",
    "  2. hash = FNV-1a 64-bit, mask Long.MAX_VALUE (0x7FFFFFFFFFFFFFFF)",
    "  3. sort variationWeights by variationKey ascending",
    "  4. totalWeight = Σ weight (Long sum to avoid Int overflow on pathological weight sets)",
    "  5. bucket = hash mod totalWeight",
    "  6. walk sorted weights, accumulating cumulative; first cumulative > bucket wins",
    "",
    "Reference values were generated by running the algorithm against the",
    "Kotlin implementation. If the spec changes, regenerate ALL `expected*`",
    "fields in the same commit and update both test files together — do not",
    "ship a fixture whose expected values were computed by only one side."
  ],
